'' =================================================================================================
''
''   File....... test_hub75_morphMask.spin2
''   Purpose.... Board test of the figure's coverage masks: shape, symmetry, exact edge pixels, total coverage, refusals
''   Authors.... Stephen M Moraco
''               -- see below for terms of use
''   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... Oct 2026
''   Updated.... 14 Oct 2026
''
'' =================================================================================================

{ Tasks 165 and 180: proves isp_hub75_morphMask on the P2. The masks are pure arithmetic, so the display is
  not started.

  Expected values come from paths independent of the code under test: the exact pixels below were worked out
  by hand from the coverage rule, and each total is checked against the piece's area by formula.

  The rule (isp_hub75_morphMask): a pixel's byte is 255 x clamp(T/2 + 1/2 - d, 0, 1), d the distance from the
  pixel's centre to the piece's centre line.
    Straight, T 3, L 20 (centre line y 1.5, x 1.5 .. 18.5; 20 columns):
      row 0 col 0: d = sqrt(1 + 1) = 1.414, 2 - 1.414 = 0.586  -> 149;  row 1 col 0: d = 1 -> 255
    Straight, T 4, L 20 (an even stroke: y 2, x 2.5 .. 18.5; 21 columns):
      row 0 col 0: d = sqrt(4 + 2.25) = 2.5 -> 0;  row 0 col 1: d = sqrt(1 + 2.25) = 1.803 -> 0.697 -> 178;
      row 1 col 0: d = sqrt(4 + 0.25) = 2.062 -> 0.438 -> 112
    Tube, T 9: the edge row at d = 4 is fully covered, weighted 1 - 0.6 x (4 / 4.5)^2 = 0.526 -> 134
    Arc, T 3 (radius 2, centre at the 4 x 4 mask's bottom-right pixel centre, 3.5, 3.5):
      row 0 col 3: d = |3 - 2| = 1 -> 255;  row 0 col 2: d = |sqrt(1 + 9) - 2| = 1.162 -> 0.838 -> 214;
      row 3 col 3 (the centre): d = 2 -> 0;  row 0 col 0: d = |4.243 - 2| -> 0
    Arc, T 4 (radius 2.5, a 5 x 5 mask, centre 4.5, 4.5):
      row 0 col 4: d = 1.5 -> 255;  row 3 col 3: d = |1.414 - 2.5| = 1.086 -> 255 (the inner edge is round)
    Arc, T 1 (radius 1, a 2 x 2 mask): its corner pixel is morphMask.THIN_CORNER_LEVEL, set by eye (Stephen,
      2026-10-14); the other three are 255, 255 and 0 (the circle's centre)
    Dot, side 2: every pixel at d = 0.707 -> 0.793 -> 202
  Areas: a straight run is a capsule, (L - T) x T + pi T^2 / 4; a dot is a disc, pi D^2 / 4.
  The figure's buffer, T 3, L 20, dot 3: straight 3 x 20 = 60, join 3 x 7 = 21, arc 4 x 4 = 16, dot 9: the join
  at 60, the arc at 81, the dot at 97, 106 bytes in all.

  Falsification: compile with -D MORPH_BREAK_MASK and every built figure has its first byte changed, and every
  refused call has a byte written into the buffer. That run must show FAIL for the exact-pixel, symmetry and
  buffer-untouched checks.
}

CON ' ---- Timing ----

  CLK_FREQ = 335_000_000                                        ' system freq as a constant
  _clkfreq = CLK_FREQ                                           ' set system clock

CON ' ---- Mask buffer ----

  MASK_BYTES = 2048                                             ' the group's buffer size
  SENTINEL = $A5                                                ' the buffer is filled with this before a call that must be refused
  SECOND_PIXEL = 1                                              ' the index of the second pixel of a row or column
  STEP_IN = 1                                                   ' one pixel in from the last index: the pixel inside a round end or bend
  HALF_DIVISOR = 2                                              ' adds half a step before dividing, to round to nearest
  BREAK_BITS = $10                                              ' -D MORPH_BREAK_MASK: XOR-ed into each built figure's first byte
  NONE_DIFFER = 0                                               ' the expected count of pixels that differ, are partly lit or were written
  DARK_LEVEL = 0                                                ' the expected byte of a pixel the shape does not cover

CON ' ---- Cases ----

  ' A: the 2021 stroke: thickness 1, every pixel of the run fully lit
  THIN_THICKNESS = 1
  THIN_LENGTH = 12
  THIN_ARC_SIDE = 2

  ' B: thickness 3 (odd)
  THREE_THICKNESS = 3
  THREE_LENGTH = 20
  THREE_COLUMNS = 20
  THREE_CORNER_LEVEL = 149
  THREE_AREA_X10 = 581                                          ' 17 x 3 + pi x 9 / 4 = 58.07 px^2, x 10
  JOIN_OFFSET_THREE = 60                                        ' the figure's layout at T 3, L 20, dot 3 (see above)
  ARC_OFFSET_THREE = 81
  DOT_OFFSET_THREE = 97
  FIGURE_BYTES_THREE = 106
  JOIN_COLUMNS_THREE = 7

  ' C: thickness 4 (even: the run starts half a pixel in)
  FOUR_THICKNESS = 4
  FOUR_LENGTH = 20
  FOUR_COLUMNS = 21
  FOUR_ROW0_COL1_LEVEL = 178
  FOUR_ROW1_COL0_LEVEL = 112
  FOUR_AREA_X10 = 766                                           ' 16 x 4 + pi x 16 / 4 = 76.57 px^2, x 10

  ' D, E: thickness 9, length 60, flat then tube
  NINE_THICKNESS = 9
  NINE_LENGTH = 60
  NINE_COLUMNS = 60
  NINE_AREA_X10 = 5226                                          ' 51 x 9 + pi x 81 / 4 = 522.62 px^2, x 10
  NINE_FIRST_FULL_COLUMN = 5                                    ' columns 5 .. 54 lie wholly between the round ends
  NINE_CENTER_ROW = 4
  TUBE_EDGE_ROW_LEVEL = 134
  MID_COLUMN = 30

  ' F, G: the arcs
  ARC_THREE_SIDE = 4
  ARC_THREE_ROW0_COL2_LEVEL = 214
  ARC_FOUR_SIDE = 5

  ' H: dots
  DOT_SMALL = 2
  DOT_SMALL_LEVEL = 202
  DOT_LARGE = 9
  DOT_LARGE_AREA_X10 = 636                                      ' pi x 81 / 4 = 63.62 px^2, x 10

  ' refusals
  BAD_THICKNESS = 0
  OVER_THICKNESS = 10
  UNDER_LENGTH = 9                                              ' shorter than the 10-pixel stroke
  UNKNOWN_SECTION = 7                                           ' no cross-section has this value

  ' totals are compared x 10 so tenths of a pixel stay whole numbers; within 1% of the area
  AREA_SCALE = 10
  PERCENT_WHOLE = 100

OBJ

    utils       : "test_hub75_morphUtils"
    morphMask   : "isp_hub75_morphMask"
    morphStatus : "isp_hub75_morphStatus"

VAR

    byte    mask[MASK_BYTES]

PUB go()
'' Run the mask test: each case, then the layout and the refusals.
''

    utils.beginSuite(@"morphMask figure masks")
    checkThin()
    checkThree()
    checkFour()
    checkNine()
    checkTube()
    checkArcs()
    checkThinArc()
    checkDots()
    checkLayout()
    checkRefusals()
    utils.finish()

PRI checkThin() | status
' Check case A, the 2021 stroke (thickness 1): it builds, has 12 columns, and every pixel is fully lit.

' Local Variables:
' @local status - build()'s result

    status := build(THIN_THICKNESS, THIN_LENGTH, THIN_THICKNESS, morphMask.SECTION_FLAT)
    utils.checkEqual(status, @"A: build thickness 1, length 12", morphStatus.SUCCESS)
    utils.checkEqual(morphMask.straightColumns(THIN_THICKNESS, THIN_LENGTH), @"A: the run has 12 columns", THIN_LENGTH)
    utils.checkEqual(partialPixels(@mask, THIN_LENGTH, THIN_THICKNESS, 0, THIN_LENGTH - morphMask.LAST_OFFSET), @"A: every pixel of the 2021 stroke fully lit", NONE_DIFFER)

PRI checkThree() | status
' Check case B (thickness 3, odd): the hand-worked end pixels, symmetry, a full interior and the capsule's area.

' Local Variables:
' @local status - build()'s result

    status := build(THREE_THICKNESS, THREE_LENGTH, THREE_THICKNESS, morphMask.SECTION_FLAT)
    utils.checkEqual(status, @"B: build thickness 3, length 20", morphStatus.SUCCESS)
    utils.checkEqual(morphMask.straightColumns(THREE_THICKNESS, THREE_LENGTH), @"B: the run has 20 columns", THREE_COLUMNS)
    utils.checkEqual(pixelAt(@mask, THREE_COLUMNS, 0, 0), @"B: the round end's corner pixel (hand-worked)", THREE_CORNER_LEVEL)
    utils.checkEqual(pixelAt(@mask, THREE_COLUMNS, SECOND_PIXEL, 0), @"B: the end pixel on the centre line is full", morphMask.COVER_FULL)
    utils.checkEqual(asymmetricPixels(@mask, THREE_COLUMNS, THREE_THICKNESS), @"B: symmetric end to end and side to side", NONE_DIFFER)
    utils.checkEqual(partialPixels(@mask, THREE_COLUMNS, THREE_THICKNESS, SECOND_PIXEL, THREE_COLUMNS - morphMask.LAST_OFFSET - STEP_IN), @"B: the interior is all 255", NONE_DIFFER)
    checkArea(@mask, THREE_COLUMNS * THREE_THICKNESS, THREE_AREA_X10, @"B: total coverage is the capsule's area within 1%")

PRI checkFour() | status
' Check case C (thickness 4, even: the run starts half a pixel in): the hand-worked pixels, symmetry and the capsule's area.

' Local Variables:
' @local status - build()'s result

    status := build(FOUR_THICKNESS, FOUR_LENGTH, FOUR_THICKNESS, morphMask.SECTION_FLAT)
    utils.checkEqual(status, @"C: build thickness 4, length 20", morphStatus.SUCCESS)
    utils.checkEqual(morphMask.straightColumns(FOUR_THICKNESS, FOUR_LENGTH), @"C: the run has 21 columns (half a pixel each end)", FOUR_COLUMNS)
    utils.checkEqual(pixelAt(@mask, FOUR_COLUMNS, 0, 0), @"C: the corner pixel is dark (hand-worked)", DARK_LEVEL)
    utils.checkEqual(pixelAt(@mask, FOUR_COLUMNS, 0, SECOND_PIXEL), @"C: row 0, column 1 (hand-worked)", FOUR_ROW0_COL1_LEVEL)
    utils.checkEqual(pixelAt(@mask, FOUR_COLUMNS, SECOND_PIXEL, 0), @"C: row 1, column 0 (hand-worked)", FOUR_ROW1_COL0_LEVEL)
    utils.checkEqual(asymmetricPixels(@mask, FOUR_COLUMNS, FOUR_THICKNESS), @"C: symmetric end to end and side to side", NONE_DIFFER)
    checkArea(@mask, FOUR_COLUMNS * FOUR_THICKNESS, FOUR_AREA_X10, @"C: total coverage is the capsule's area within 1%")

PRI checkNine() | status
' Check case D (thickness 9, length 60, flat): symmetry, a full interior and the capsule's area.

' Local Variables:
' @local status - build()'s result

    status := build(NINE_THICKNESS, NINE_LENGTH, NINE_THICKNESS, morphMask.SECTION_FLAT)
    utils.checkEqual(status, @"D: build thickness 9, length 60", morphStatus.SUCCESS)
    utils.checkEqual(asymmetricPixels(@mask, NINE_COLUMNS, NINE_THICKNESS), @"D: symmetric end to end and side to side", NONE_DIFFER)
    utils.checkEqual(partialPixels(@mask, NINE_COLUMNS, NINE_THICKNESS, NINE_FIRST_FULL_COLUMN, NINE_COLUMNS - NINE_FIRST_FULL_COLUMN - morphMask.LAST_OFFSET), @"D: the interior is all 255", NONE_DIFFER)
    checkArea(@mask, NINE_COLUMNS * NINE_THICKNESS, NINE_AREA_X10, @"D: total coverage is the capsule's area within 1%")

PRI checkTube() | status
' Check case E (thickness 9, length 60, tube): the centre line is full, the edge row has its hand-worked weight, and it is symmetric.

' Local Variables:
' @local status - build()'s result

    status := build(NINE_THICKNESS, NINE_LENGTH, NINE_THICKNESS, morphMask.SECTION_TUBE)
    utils.checkEqual(status, @"E: build thickness 9, length 60, tube", morphStatus.SUCCESS)
    utils.checkEqual(pixelAt(@mask, NINE_COLUMNS, NINE_CENTER_ROW, MID_COLUMN), @"E: the centre line is fully lit", morphMask.COVER_FULL)
    utils.checkEqual(pixelAt(@mask, NINE_COLUMNS, 0, MID_COLUMN), @"E: the edge row's weight (hand-worked)", TUBE_EDGE_ROW_LEVEL)
    utils.checkEqual(asymmetricPixels(@mask, NINE_COLUMNS, NINE_THICKNESS), @"E: symmetric end to end and side to side", NONE_DIFFER)

PRI checkArcs() | status, pArc
' Check cases F and G, the arcs at thickness 3 and 4: their hand-worked pixels, a round bend and symmetry across the diagonal.

' Local Variables:
' @local status - build()'s result
' @local pArc - the address of the arc in the figure's buffer

    status := build(THREE_THICKNESS, THREE_LENGTH, THREE_THICKNESS, morphMask.SECTION_FLAT)
    pArc := @mask + morphMask.arcOffset(THREE_THICKNESS, THREE_LENGTH)
    utils.checkEqual(morphMask.arcSide(THREE_THICKNESS), @"F: the arc at thickness 3 is 4 x 4", ARC_THREE_SIDE)
    utils.checkEqual(pixelAt(pArc, ARC_THREE_SIDE, 0, ARC_THREE_SIDE - morphMask.LAST_OFFSET), @"F: its top end, on the centre line, is full", morphMask.COVER_FULL)
    utils.checkEqual(pixelAt(pArc, ARC_THREE_SIDE, 0, ARC_THREE_SIDE - morphMask.LAST_OFFSET - STEP_IN), @"F: row 0, column 2 (hand-worked)", ARC_THREE_ROW0_COL2_LEVEL)
    utils.checkEqual(pixelAt(pArc, ARC_THREE_SIDE, ARC_THREE_SIDE - morphMask.LAST_OFFSET, ARC_THREE_SIDE - morphMask.LAST_OFFSET), @"F: the circle's centre pixel is dark", DARK_LEVEL)
    utils.checkEqual(pixelAt(pArc, ARC_THREE_SIDE, 0, 0), @"F: the outer corner is dark: the corner is round", DARK_LEVEL)
    utils.checkEqual(untransposedPixels(pArc, ARC_THREE_SIDE), @"F: the same across its diagonal (both ends alike)", NONE_DIFFER)

    status := build(FOUR_THICKNESS, FOUR_LENGTH, FOUR_THICKNESS, morphMask.SECTION_FLAT)
    pArc := @mask + morphMask.arcOffset(FOUR_THICKNESS, FOUR_LENGTH)
    utils.checkEqual(pixelAt(pArc, ARC_FOUR_SIDE, 0, ARC_FOUR_SIDE - morphMask.LAST_OFFSET), @"G: thickness 4: its top end is full", morphMask.COVER_FULL)
    utils.checkEqual(pixelAt(pArc, ARC_FOUR_SIDE, ARC_FOUR_SIDE - morphMask.LAST_OFFSET - STEP_IN, ARC_FOUR_SIDE - morphMask.LAST_OFFSET - STEP_IN), @"G: the pixel inside the bend is full (its inner edge is round)", morphMask.COVER_FULL)
    utils.checkEqual(pixelAt(pArc, ARC_FOUR_SIDE, ARC_FOUR_SIDE - morphMask.LAST_OFFSET, ARC_FOUR_SIDE - morphMask.LAST_OFFSET), @"G: the circle's centre pixel is dark", DARK_LEVEL)
    utils.checkEqual(untransposedPixels(pArc, ARC_FOUR_SIDE), @"G: the same across its diagonal", NONE_DIFFER)

PRI checkThinArc() | status, pArc
' Check case I, the arc at thickness 1: the dimmed corner, the two full step pixels and the dark inside pixel.

' Local Variables:
' @local status - build()'s result
' @local pArc - the address of the arc in the figure's buffer

    status := build(THIN_THICKNESS, THIN_LENGTH, THIN_THICKNESS, morphMask.SECTION_FLAT)
    pArc := @mask + morphMask.arcOffset(THIN_THICKNESS, THIN_LENGTH)
    utils.checkEqual(pixelAt(pArc, THIN_ARC_SIDE, 0, 0), @"I: stroke 1: the corner pixel is dimmed (by eye)", morphMask.THIN_CORNER_LEVEL)
    utils.checkEqual(pixelAt(pArc, THIN_ARC_SIDE, 0, SECOND_PIXEL) + pixelAt(pArc, THIN_ARC_SIDE, SECOND_PIXEL, 0), @"I: its two step pixels are full", morphMask.COVER_FULL + morphMask.COVER_FULL)
    utils.checkEqual(pixelAt(pArc, THIN_ARC_SIDE, SECOND_PIXEL, SECOND_PIXEL), @"I: its inside pixel is dark", DARK_LEVEL)

PRI checkDots() | status, pDot
' Check case H, the colon dots: a 2-pixel dot's hand-worked pixels, and a 9-pixel dot's roundness and disc area.

' Local Variables:
' @local status - build()'s result
' @local pDot - the address of the dot in the figure's buffer

    status := build(THREE_THICKNESS, THREE_LENGTH, DOT_SMALL, morphMask.SECTION_FLAT)
    pDot := @mask + morphMask.dotOffset(THREE_THICKNESS, THREE_LENGTH)
    utils.checkEqual(pixelAt(pDot, DOT_SMALL, 0, 0) + pixelAt(pDot, DOT_SMALL, SECOND_PIXEL, SECOND_PIXEL), @"H: a 2-pixel dot: its pixels (hand-worked)", DOT_SMALL_LEVEL + DOT_SMALL_LEVEL)
    status := build(NINE_THICKNESS, NINE_LENGTH, DOT_LARGE, morphMask.SECTION_FLAT)
    pDot := @mask + morphMask.dotOffset(NINE_THICKNESS, NINE_LENGTH)
    utils.checkEqual(asymmetricPixels(pDot, DOT_LARGE, DOT_LARGE) + untransposedPixels(pDot, DOT_LARGE), @"H: a 9-pixel dot is round: symmetric every way", NONE_DIFFER)
    checkArea(pDot, DOT_LARGE * DOT_LARGE, DOT_LARGE_AREA_X10, @"H: its total coverage is the disc's area within 1%")

PRI checkLayout() | pJoin
' Check the figure's layout at thickness 3, length 20: where the join, arc and dot start, its size, and the join's pixels.

' Local Variables:
' @local pJoin - the address of the join in the figure's buffer

    utils.checkEqual(morphMask.joinOffset(THREE_THICKNESS, THREE_LENGTH), @"layout: the join follows the straight run", JOIN_OFFSET_THREE)
    utils.checkEqual(morphMask.arcOffset(THREE_THICKNESS, THREE_LENGTH), @"layout: the arc follows the join", ARC_OFFSET_THREE)
    utils.checkEqual(morphMask.dotOffset(THREE_THICKNESS, THREE_LENGTH), @"layout: the dot follows the arc", DOT_OFFSET_THREE)
    utils.checkEqual(morphMask.figureBytes(THREE_THICKNESS, THREE_LENGTH, THREE_THICKNESS), @"layout: the figure's bytes", FIGURE_BYTES_THREE)
    build(THREE_THICKNESS, THREE_LENGTH, THREE_THICKNESS, morphMask.SECTION_FLAT)
    pJoin := @mask + JOIN_OFFSET_THREE
    utils.checkEqual(morphMask.joinColumns(THREE_THICKNESS), @"layout: the join has 7 columns (a centre line of 4)", JOIN_COLUMNS_THREE)
    utils.checkEqual(pixelAt(pJoin, JOIN_COLUMNS_THREE, 0, 0), @"layout: the join has the straight run's round end", THREE_CORNER_LEVEL)
    utils.checkEqual(asymmetricPixels(pJoin, JOIN_COLUMNS_THREE, THREE_THICKNESS), @"layout: the join is symmetric", NONE_DIFFER)

PRI checkRefusals() | status
' Check that buildFigure() refuses bad arguments (each with its own status, writing nothing) and accepts the limit.

' Local Variables:
' @local status - buildFigure()'s result

    ' a stroke or a dot needs at least one pixel, so a thickness or a dot of 0 must be refused with E_BAD_THICKNESS
    checkRefused(BAD_THICKNESS, THREE_LENGTH, THREE_THICKNESS, morphMask.SECTION_FLAT, MASK_BYTES, morphStatus.E_BAD_THICKNESS, @"refuse thickness 0")
    checkRefused(THREE_THICKNESS, THREE_LENGTH, 0, morphMask.SECTION_FLAT, MASK_BYTES, morphStatus.E_BAD_THICKNESS, @"refuse a dot of 0")
    ' a stroke thicker than its length cannot be drawn: E_THICKNESS_TOO_LARGE
    checkRefused(OVER_THICKNESS, UNDER_LENGTH, OVER_THICKNESS, morphMask.SECTION_FLAT, MASK_BYTES, morphStatus.E_THICKNESS_TOO_LARGE, @"refuse thickness 10 on length 9")
    ' no cross-section has the value UNKNOWN_SECTION: E_UNKNOWN_CROSS_SECTION
    checkRefused(THREE_THICKNESS, THREE_LENGTH, THREE_THICKNESS, UNKNOWN_SECTION, MASK_BYTES, morphStatus.E_UNKNOWN_CROSS_SECTION, @"refuse an unknown cross-section")
    ' the figure needs FIGURE_BYTES_THREE bytes; one byte fewer must be refused with E_MASK_TOO_LARGE
    checkRefused(THREE_THICKNESS, THREE_LENGTH, THREE_THICKNESS, morphMask.SECTION_FLAT, FIGURE_BYTES_THREE - morphMask.LAST_OFFSET, morphStatus.E_MASK_TOO_LARGE, @"refuse a buffer one byte too small")
    status := morphMask.buildFigure(@mask, MASK_BYTES, OVER_THICKNESS, OVER_THICKNESS, OVER_THICKNESS, morphMask.SECTION_FLAT)
    utils.checkEqual(status, @"accept thickness 10 on length 10 (not greater)", morphStatus.SUCCESS)

PRI checkRefused(thickness, length, dotSize, crossSection, capacity, expectedStatus, pName) | status, idx, changed
' Check that buildFigure() refuses a call with the expected status and writes nothing into a buffer pre-filled with SENTINEL.
'
' @param thickness - the stroke thickness in pixels
' @param length - the segment length in pixels
' @param dotSize - the colon dot's side in pixels
' @param crossSection - the cross-section (morphMask.SECTION_ value)
' @param capacity - the buffer size given to buildFigure(), in bytes
' @param expectedStatus - the status buildFigure() must return
' @param pName - zero-terminated name of the check

' Local Variables:
' @local status - buildFigure()'s result
' @local idx - the buffer byte being examined
' @local changed - how many buffer bytes no longer hold SENTINEL

    bytefill(@mask, SENTINEL, MASK_BYTES)
    status := morphMask.buildFigure(@mask, capacity, thickness, length, dotSize, crossSection)
#IFDEF MORPH_BREAK_MASK
    mask[0] := 0
#ENDIF
    utils.checkEqual(status, pName, expectedStatus)
    changed := 0
    repeat idx from 0 to MASK_BYTES - morphMask.LAST_OFFSET
        if mask[idx] <> SENTINEL
            changed++
    utils.checkEqual(changed, @"  ... and writes nothing (bytes changed)", NONE_DIFFER)

PRI build(thickness, length, dotSize, crossSection) : status
' Build the figure into the full buffer; the falsification build then damages the result.
'
' @param thickness - the stroke thickness in pixels
' @param length - the segment length in pixels
' @param dotSize - the colon dot's side in pixels
' @param crossSection - the cross-section (morphMask.SECTION_ value)
' @returns status - buildFigure()'s result

    status := morphMask.buildFigure(@mask, MASK_BYTES, thickness, length, dotSize, crossSection)
#IFDEF MORPH_BREAK_MASK
    mask[0] ^= BREAK_BITS
#ENDIF

PRI pixelAt(pMask, nCols, row, col) : level
' Read one pixel's coverage byte from a mask.
'
' @param pMask - the address of the mask's first byte
' @param nCols - the mask's width in pixels
' @param row - the pixel's row
' @param col - the pixel's column
' @returns level - the pixel's coverage (0 to morphMask.COVER_FULL)

    level := BYTE[pMask][row * nCols + col]

PRI asymmetricPixels(pMask, nCols, nRows) : nDiffer | row, col
' Count the pixels that differ from their mirror end to end, or from their mirror side to side.
'
' @param pMask - the address of the mask's first byte
' @param nCols - the mask's width in pixels
' @param nRows - the mask's height in pixels
' @returns nDiffer - how many pixels differ from a mirror
'
' Local Variables:
' @local row - the pixel's row
' @local col - the pixel's column

    nDiffer := 0
    repeat row from 0 to nRows - morphMask.LAST_OFFSET
        repeat col from 0 to nCols - morphMask.LAST_OFFSET
            if pixelAt(pMask, nCols, row, col) <> pixelAt(pMask, nCols, row, nCols - morphMask.LAST_OFFSET - col) or pixelAt(pMask, nCols, row, col) <> pixelAt(pMask, nCols, nRows - morphMask.LAST_OFFSET - row, col)
                nDiffer++

PRI untransposedPixels(pMask, side) : nDiffer | row, col
' Count the pixels of a square mask that differ from their mirror across the diagonal.
'
' @param pMask - the address of the mask's first byte
' @param side - the square mask's side in pixels
' @returns nDiffer - how many pixels differ from a mirror
'
' Local Variables:
' @local row - the pixel's row
' @local col - the pixel's column

    nDiffer := 0
    repeat row from 0 to side - morphMask.LAST_OFFSET
        repeat col from 0 to side - morphMask.LAST_OFFSET
            if pixelAt(pMask, side, row, col) <> pixelAt(pMask, side, col, row)
                nDiffer++

PRI partialPixels(pMask, nCols, nRows, firstCol, lastCol) : nPartial | row, col
' Count the pixels in columns firstCol..lastCol (every row) that are not fully lit.
'
' @param pMask - the address of the mask's first byte
' @param nCols - the mask's width in pixels
' @param nRows - the mask's height in pixels
' @param firstCol - the first column counted
' @param lastCol - the last column counted
' @returns nPartial - how many of those pixels are not fully lit
'
' Local Variables:
' @local row - the pixel's row
' @local col - the pixel's column

    nPartial := 0
    repeat row from 0 to nRows - morphMask.LAST_OFFSET
        repeat col from firstCol to lastCol
            if pixelAt(pMask, nCols, row, col) <> morphMask.COVER_FULL
                nPartial++

PRI checkArea(pMask, nBytes, areaX10, pName) | total, idx, totalX10
' Sum a mask, in pixels x 10, and check it is within 1% of the shape's area.
'
' @param pMask - the address of the mask's first byte
' @param nBytes - how many mask bytes to sum
' @param areaX10 - the shape's area by formula, in tenths of a pixel
' @param pName - zero-terminated name of the check
'
' Local Variables:
' @local total - the sum of the coverage bytes
' @local idx - the mask byte being added
' @local totalX10 - the summed coverage in tenths of a pixel

    total := 0
    repeat idx from 0 to nBytes - morphMask.LAST_OFFSET
        total += BYTE[pMask][idx]
    totalX10 := (total * AREA_SCALE + morphMask.COVER_FULL / HALF_DIVISOR) / morphMask.COVER_FULL
    debug("AREA     ", zstr_(pName), "  total_x10=", sdec_(totalX10), "  area_x10=", sdec_(areaX10))
    utils.checkEqual(abs (totalX10 - areaX10) * PERCENT_WHOLE <= areaX10, pName, TRUE)

CON ' ---- License ----

